    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1068-2781"
  - family-names: Bouzinier
    given-names: Michael
    email: michael.bouzinier@forome.org
    affiliation: Harvard University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3161-5601"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ForomePlatform/synthetic-resdac-claims"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - medicare
  - resdac
  - synthetic-data
  - claims
  - medpar
  - mbsf
abstract: >-
  synthmed is a Python package that generates synthetic ResDAC /
  Medicare claims data (MEDPAR, MBSF) as fixed-width DAT files conforming
  to a set of ResDAC File Transfer Specification (FTS) schemas.  It
  maintains a single internal cohort of synthetic beneficiaries and
  rolls it forward year-by-year so that demographics, IDs, locations,
  and diagnosis histories stay consistent across files; realistic
  data-quality errors are injected on the way through.

